  "result": "Perfect! All 88 tests pass. I've successfully added VAT calculation support throughout the invoicing system.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/invoices.js** - Added VAT calculations:\n   - `lineVat(line)` - Calculates VAT on the net amount after discount: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) * vatRate / 100`, rounded with `roundCents()`\n   - Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }` where:\n     - `vat` is the sum of all line VATs\n     - `total = subtotal - discount + vat`, clamped at 0\n\n2. **src/render.js** - Updated to display VAT:\n   - Shows VAT on a separate line (only if VAT > 0)\n   - Displays final total including VAT\n   - Updated totals calculation to use `invoiceTotals()`\n\n3. **Tests** - Added 8 new tests covering:\n   - VAT calculation on net amounts after discount\n   - Different VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n   - Multiple lines with VAT summing\n   - VAT rendering in plain text\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- VAT is computed per line on the discounted amount, then summed (not a percentage of total)\n- Rounding happens per line, so total VAT is sum of rounded line VATs\n- VAT is omitted from rendering when zero (VAT-exempt items)",
